retrieval time required.

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.700
So we think that
our storage is going

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.540
to be a better value
for online data,

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:52.300
whether it's hot or
cold, whether you've

00:18:52.300 --> 00:18:55.040
got millisecond access
time that you need

00:18:55.040 --> 00:18:57.130
globally reliable, or less.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.780
Coldline is a highly
available, affordable solution

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:08.150
for backup, archival,
and disaster recovery.

00:19:08.150 --> 00:19:09.800
It really is incredible.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:14.410
We offer you the speed of
disk at the cost of tape.

00:19:18.156 --> 00:19:19.530
But you might be
asking yourself,

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.960
how am I going to get all
my data up into the cloud?

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:24.690
Well, for that, we just launched
something about last month

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:25.940
called the Transfer Appliance.

00:19:25.940 --> 00:19:28.190
This is a physical
appliance that we rent you

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:29.540
for a window of time.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:31.880
You load your data onto it,
and then you send it back

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.650
to us using a courier.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:36.210
The capacity for this is
up to 1 petabit compressed.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:39.500
It's the largest transfer
appliance in the cloud.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:42.300
Because a lot of our customers
are moving a lot of data to us,

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.215
and we wanted to give
them as much capacity

00:19:44.215 --> 00:19:45.090
as we possibly could.

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.699
The Transfer Appliance
is all about speed.

00:19:51.699 --> 00:19:53.240
In this animation,
what you're seeing

00:19:53.240 --> 00:19:55.610
is how fast it would take
a Transfer Appliance to be

00:19:55.610 --> 00:19:57.434
shipped out to you,
for you to fill it up,

00:19:57.434 --> 00:19:58.850
and for you to
send it back to us,

00:19:58.850 --> 00:20:00.740
and us to load it into
Google Cloud Storage.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:02.510
On average, 43 days.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.330
If you compare that over
a typical network, which

00:20:05.330 --> 00:20:07.490
is 100 megabits
per second, it is

00:20:07.490 --> 00:20:11.610
going to take a lot
longer than 43 days.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.580
As you can see, it will
take multiple years--

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:14.720
like more than three years.

00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:22.300
Let's talk about what
we're doing for support.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:23.905
Support hasn't evolved.

00:20:27.260 --> 00:20:29.060
What we are doing to
evolve it is we're

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:31.970
offering role-based support.

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:35.570
What this means is that you
pay a flat price per user,

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:39.290
per month, as opposed
to a percentage fee

00:20:39.290 --> 00:20:41.220
uplift on your cloud usage.

00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:44.030
So you might be accustomed to
paying a certain percentage,

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:48.290
like 10%, to 20%, to 30%
uplift on your cloud usage.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:51.440
We are evolving that to this
new method, where you pay

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:53.790
a flat fee per user per month.

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.322
So let's take an example.

00:20:55.322 --> 00:20:56.780
Let's say that
you're a development

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:58.940
shop with 10
engineers, that would

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:03.050
be 10 engineers multiplied
by $100 per user

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:04.940
per month, multiplied by 12.

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:07.910
So that's $12,000
in annual support

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.720
for this development shop, which
is likely much, much less--

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:14.120
and certainly, much,
much more predictable

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:17.600
than if you were to pay a flat
percentage fee on your cloud

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:18.200
bill.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.140
It also is a lot closer to
getting a value for your money

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:22.910
because we're charging
you per engineer,

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:24.920
as opposed to charging
you a percentage uplift.

00:21:29.490 --> 00:21:31.980
The old model, we
call account-based.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.990
The new model, we
call role-based.

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:36.780
Account-based, you're accustomed
to long-term contracts,

00:21:36.780 --> 00:21:38.790
standardized tiers,
and like I said,

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:40.980
percentage-based uplift
on your cloud bill.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:43.800
With role-based, you've got
a very flexible environment

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.650
that you can change month to
month, no commitments, very

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:48.060
customizable configurations.

00:21:48.060 --> 00:21:51.980
You tell us how
many users you want.

00:21:51.980 --> 00:21:53.790
And it's very predictable,
because you know

00:21:53.790 --> 00:21:54.998
how many users you're buying.

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:00.980
This is coming very
soon, and we're

00:22:00.980 --> 00:22:02.600
