00:26:29.569 --> 00:26:31.860
The first one is-- where did
the idea for sustained use

00:26:31.860 --> 00:26:34.350
discounts come from?

00:26:34.350 --> 00:26:37.142
It predates me here at Google.

00:26:37.142 --> 00:26:38.850
I came up with the
lunch counter example,

00:26:38.850 --> 00:26:40.620
because I eat sandwiches.

00:26:40.620 --> 00:26:44.160
And when I buy 10 of them,
I get a free sandwich.

00:26:44.160 --> 00:26:46.397
And it sounds a lot like
sustained use discounts.

00:26:46.397 --> 00:26:48.480
The big difference between
sustained use discounts

00:26:48.480 --> 00:26:50.400
and the lunch counter
is that I'm always

00:26:50.400 --> 00:26:52.680
forgetting my little
card and losing it.

00:26:52.680 --> 00:26:56.070
And that never happens, because
we keep track of it for you.

00:26:56.070 --> 00:26:57.630
Question 2.

00:26:57.630 --> 00:27:01.080
Are GCP pricing innovations
only for compute?

00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:02.880
Many of them are for compute.

00:27:02.880 --> 00:27:05.880
Rightsizing recommendations,
sustained use discount,

00:27:05.880 --> 00:27:06.870
committed use discount.

00:27:06.870 --> 00:27:09.600
Those are for compute.

00:27:09.600 --> 00:27:11.640
However, many of them are not.

00:27:11.640 --> 00:27:15.090
For example, Coldline-- where
we offer you the speed of disk

00:27:15.090 --> 00:27:17.490
at the cost of tape--

00:27:17.490 --> 00:27:19.920
is very innovative and is
a storage innovation, not

00:27:19.920 --> 00:27:21.150
a computer innovation.

00:27:21.150 --> 00:27:24.630
Network service tiers also
is the opportunity for you

00:27:24.630 --> 00:27:28.260
to experience 70% faster
networks than the average cloud

00:27:28.260 --> 00:27:32.160
provider, or 9% lower costs.

00:27:32.160 --> 00:27:36.300
And that's a
networking innovation.

00:27:36.300 --> 00:27:37.770
Question number 3.

00:27:37.770 --> 00:27:40.530
Can I change my instance
sizes and still receive

00:27:40.530 --> 00:27:42.090
committed use discounts?

00:27:42.090 --> 00:27:42.960
Yes.

00:27:42.960 --> 00:27:44.340
Unlike other cloud
providers that

00:27:44.340 --> 00:27:49.420
offer you committed use discount
structures that are inflexible,

00:27:49.420 --> 00:27:50.610
our are flexible.

00:27:50.610 --> 00:27:52.700
So you buy a certain
amount of CPU

00:27:52.700 --> 00:27:54.210
and a certain amount of memory.

00:27:54.210 --> 00:27:57.510
And within that
bundle, that basket,

00:27:57.510 --> 00:27:59.850
you can change exactly the
kind of VM configurations

00:27:59.850 --> 00:28:02.040
that you want from
minute to minute, day

00:28:02.040 --> 00:28:08.520
to day within that month,
within that year-- whether it's

00:28:08.520 --> 00:28:11.970
a one year or three year
committed use discount.

00:28:11.970 --> 00:28:13.410
Question 4.

00:28:13.410 --> 00:28:18.420
What is the difference
between SUDs and CUDs?

00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:20.670
Sustained use
discount, let's see

00:28:20.670 --> 00:28:23.100
if I can think of
a funny analogy.

00:28:23.100 --> 00:28:25.950
Sustained use discount is when
you go to a lunch counter,

00:28:25.950 --> 00:28:28.280
and they give you
one of those cards.

00:28:28.280 --> 00:28:30.420
And if you eat 10
of those sandwiches,

00:28:30.420 --> 00:28:31.790
they give you a free sandwich.

00:28:31.790 --> 00:28:34.440
Committed use discounts is
when you go to the car wash

00:28:34.440 --> 00:28:36.780
and you say, I want
to buy 10 washes.

00:28:36.780 --> 00:28:38.470
I'm going to buy them right now.

00:28:38.470 --> 00:28:41.130
And then, I'm going to
use them over the next one

00:28:41.130 --> 00:28:42.270
year or three year.

00:28:42.270 --> 00:28:47.707
And as a result, you get a
cheaper rate per car wash.

00:28:47.707 --> 00:28:49.290
That analogy falls
apart a little bit,

00:28:49.290 --> 00:28:52.800
because we don't make you pay
ahead, and the car wash would.

00:28:52.800 --> 00:28:56.390
But other than that,
it's a decent analogy.

00:28:56.390 --> 00:28:57.230
Number 5.

00:28:57.230 --> 00:29:00.590
Will Rightsizing Recommendations
support all operating system

00:29:00.590 --> 00:29:03.470
